{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118718-alternative-view-on-covenants","id":1118718,"title":"Alternative view on Covenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T15:05:10-07:00","id":1118718,"title":"Alternative view on Covenants","content":"<i><b>The Covenants may be fresh the first time you play Vampire: The Requiem, but as soon as the second campaign, I felt that they start to becoming that factor that clans in Masquerate have been: They provide fast, easy to implement conflicts, but very fast they begin to turn chronicles and characters into archetypes. It\u00b4s just too easy, too seducing to use them and it all feels samey very, very fast. To mix things up by changing the stereotype deliberately feels shallow, it just doesn\u00b4t feel right.</b></i><br /> <br /> <b><i>So, here\u00b4s another, alternative view on the Covenants, that is used in my Chronicle. So far, it is fun. I thought I post it, feel free to discuss it. I am curious if you like it or not:</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First off, the majority of Vampires are not in a Covenant at all and the Covenant themselves wouldn\u00b4t want it anyway. They are not out for recruitment, they are all about isolation. Only the chosen ones may join and even then only after rigid and dangerous trials. A Covenant is an elite society, a cult of extreme ideologists. That additionally means that there are not 5 big Covenants. They are more but the members are far less numerous. In most cities, there are only a handful of Covenants if at all. And they are always different.</b><br /> <b>The Covenant mostly doesn\u00b4t care about ruling a city. They pursue their ideologies and their creed. In fact, in most cities, the vampires wouldn\u00b4t want to be ruled by them. A Covenant does not revolve about power, for them, their goal is far greater. The Invictus looks for power and control in the mortal world, the Lancea et Sanctum want to spread the faith and be the priests of their creed, the Ordo Dracul seeks transcendence, the Circle of Crone Magic and the Carthians rebellion and freedom.</b><br /> <b>For the other Vampires, they are creeps and extremists. A Prince may be member of a Covenant, but only if he\u00b4s doing his duty without letting his ideology interfere with his politics. Even if a member of a Covenant was the prince, he by far doesn\u00b4t control the city at all. If he would try to enforce his believes, the other vampires would at least try to tear him to pieces before it is too late.</b><br /> <b>But that does not mean there is no way a Covenant could not be in power, it is just an enormous feat to accomplish that. The elders must be converted or destroyed, key functions in the city must be conquered. If a Covenant is megalomanic enough to try, in 9 out of 10 cases they will be exterminated.</b><br /> <b>When a Covenant does manage to conquer a city, the repercussions are far more severe than in vanilla- Requiem. These groups have not the tolerance and the feelings for real, grounded politics. A Covenant, which has the will to power and actually archieves it would force his ideologie on all Kindred in the city. Everyone who does not bow his knees would be destroyed or exiled. Under the Lancea et Sanctum, it would turn into a Theocratie that punishes and destroys all non-believers, cities conquered by the invictus would become rigid hierarchies.<br /> <br /> <i>Thoughts and critic are invited.<br /> <br /> Keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis </i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","user":"Narr666","date":".  typo 07-20-2017, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:29:05-07:00","id":1118723,"title":"","content":"Why not just throw out the convenants completely? Just leave the basic ideological elements present in the setting without the formal power structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:38:02-07:00","id":1118726,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought about that as well. It\u00b4s a legitimate thing and maybe next time, I will even do it. <br /> <br /> But as I play in Cologne, I had an idea revolving about the Lancea Sanktum (what is Cologne without Catholics), so I thought of an idea how I can keep the Covenants without letting them dominate. And as I spend some time thinking about it, I thought it will be worth to share.<br /> <br /> But you are right, deleting the Covenants is a good way by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:51:01-07:00","id":1118730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118718-alternative-view-on-covenants?p=1118723#post1118723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just throw out the convenants completely? Just leave the basic ideological elements present in the setting without the formal power structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danse Macabre does a phenomenal job of showing how to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:11:16-07:00","id":1118744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118718-alternative-view-on-covenants?p=1118726#post1118726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I thought about that as well. It\u00b4s a legitimate thing and maybe next time, I will even do it.<br /> <br /> But as I play in Cologne, I had an idea revolving about the Lancea Sanktum (what is Cologne without Catholics), so I thought of an idea how I can keep the Covenants without letting them dominate. And as I spend some time thinking about it, I thought it will be worth to share.<br /> <br /> But you are right, deleting the Covenants is a good way by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can also just have a disproportionate amount of Unaligned Kindred in the Domain. Make the Covenants more like opt-in exclusive clubs, instead of something vampires are expected to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:26:08-07:00","id":1118750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118718-alternative-view-on-covenants?p=1118744#post1118744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can also just have a disproportionate amount of Unaligned Kindred in the Domain. Make the Covenants more like opt-in exclusive clubs, instead of something vampires are expected to join.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u00b4s in a nutshell what I presented. I gave some additional thoughts on how to view it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T18:02:37-07:00","id":1118774,"title":"","content":"It's something that's already been accounted for in the setting, there are areas where the unaligned rule and outnumber the covenants, where only one covenant exists in a small island among outsiders.<br /> <br /> Only two of the covenants really exist to force their views on others. The other three are bent more inward and not so much the converting type anyways.<br /> <br /> You might look at Danse Macabre for the variant covenants, though, they tend to be fun and can certainly spice up covenants you find boring or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T09:55:43-07:00","id":1119010,"title":"","content":"In my long-running setting, roughly half of the domain population are Unaligned, including a number of officers. Until the the Ordo were outed, it appeared the city was ruled by the Unaligned. <br /> <br /> In my new setting (complete with mostly newbie players), Covenants haven't come up. OoC, there is a member of the Ordo, several members of a death-studying covenant, and that's all I've worked up thus far. To me, covenants aren't that interesting unless there are enough members to fill them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:16:38-07:00","id":1119248,"title":"","content":"Agreed. That is the reason why I don\u00b4t use the term &quot;Unaligned&quot;, as it implies it is somewhat unusual to be not in a Covenant. In my universe, the Covenants are the odd thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:17:01-07:00","id":1119557,"title":"","content":"I'm with you all the way. I personnally removed covenants and clans from my setting. All there is are vampires and local factions (local being a generic term here). This allows far more flexibility and creativity while not stopping you at all from taking ideas from the original covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T20:16:06-07:00","id":1119748,"title":"","content":"I generally like to use the covenants because I like to structure a city, but also because I liken it less as a political organization and more as a larger coterie; sure, they might fight and squabble, but generally people won't end up dead because all of the other jerks in the city might come down on you one day. So two kindred might hate each other to the core, but they'd still fight side by side if things truly came down to it. However, I do understand how the covenants can become a bit bland when using them too much, so I'm currently working on a setting (a rural area, actually) that uses none of the covenants in the core book.<br /> <br /> I also typically have more unaligned in a given city than less because the ideals of the covenant just didn't jell with them, and generally a covenant won't go out recruiting them because there'd be little point to it. I actually don't think I've had any covenant try to go out and recruit characters in my games; generally it's the character trying to join the covenant rather than the covenant trying to get the character to join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:58:43-07:00","id":1119903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1118718-alternative-view-on-covenants?p=1118726#post1118726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I thought about that as well. It\u00b4s a legitimate thing and maybe next time, I will even do it.<br /> <br /> But as I play in Cologne, I had an idea revolving about the Lancea Sanktum (what is Cologne without Catholics), so I thought of an idea how I can keep the Covenants without letting them dominate. And as I spend some time thinking about it, I thought it will be worth to share.<br /> <br /> But you are right, deleting the Covenants is a good way by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's Lancea Sancta in Germany","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:17:56-07:00","id":1119991,"title":"","content":"Dunno, I shift things around. Patriarchy based cults in Greece's Circle; Muslim splinter of the Lacea et Sanctum; Fascistic/Neo Nazi groups within the Carthian Movement; a Kogaion that stumbled upon a secret that allowed him to out-perform even the First Estate in terms of temporal power, etc. Subverting themes doesn't requires scrapping setting elements completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}